                <pb facs="0965" n="885" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg885"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Merry to President Zelaya.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-07-19"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 19,
                    1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have telegraphed the United States consul-general at Panama not to permit
                    detention on the Isthmus of any article that may be the property of your
                    Government, and I have also written to my Government about the matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Lawrence
                    Merry.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
